Allocate chartr()'s translation-spec lists with R_alloc() so the errors
raised while building them do not leak the nodes allocated so far.

do_chartr() (src/main/character.c) built the 'old' and 'new' spec lists
with R_Calloc() and freed them by hand after building the translation
table; "decreasing range specification", "'old' is longer than 'new'"
and "invalid multibyte string" unwind past that teardown.  With the
nodes from R_alloc() the vmax reset on unwind releases them, and the
*_free_spec() helpers go away.

Found by OSS-Fuzz: testcase 5656976332488704 (libFuzzer_r_character,
Direct-leak; chartr(old = "...F-8...")).

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #368, filed 2026-10-10 (no Bugzilla
report yet).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

